content.text:
Use the `@variant` directive with a breakpoint name inside your CSS, and set the variable within it:

```css
:root {
  --my-var: 1rem;
  @variant md {
    --my-var: 2rem;
  }
}
```

The `@variant` pattern comes from `src/docs/functions-and-directives.mdx` ("@variant"), which shows `@variant dark { … }` nested inside a selector. The breakpoint names (`sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xl`, `2xl`) and their `@media (width >= …)` output come from `src/docs/responsive-design.mdx` ("Working mobile-first" and "Customizing your theme").

I adapted the `md` example from the `dark` one. The docs don't show a breakpoint inside `@variant` explicitly.

You can also write the media query yourself with `@media (width >= theme(--breakpoint-xl)) { … }`. That is shown in `src/docs/upgrade-guide.mdx`, in the section on the `theme()` function.

